		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3841&amp;p=29948#p29948"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi everyone,<br><br>I just recently dug out my Retevis RT90 after taking it out of the truck when I had an unplanned medical disability retirement back in August. Figured kind of pointless to keep a radio in a truck that sits for days a a time and gets driven only a few minutes every other day, I used to have a 45 minute commute each way when I was working prior to August 22nd 2023. Having this radio made those commutes fly by in no time.<br>So anyways, I recently updated the Open GD77CPS to the latest version, R.2024.01.22.01. I was using the Open GD77 CPS version  R.2023.08.01.01 prior to this and it would load the keps no issue and the files would be there. <br>o now I went to the latest version and when I load the keps, it says Upload Complete, AO27, AO91, CAS3H, FO11, HADES-D, ISS, PO101, SO50, TEVEL2, TEVEL3, TEVEL4, TEVEL5, TEVEL6, TEVEL7.<br>Then I go to the RT90 and enter Satellite mode, and it sits with a blank screen. After hitting the UP and Down controls I get Pass None and List Empty.<br><br>I know I'm missing something here, any ideas or suggestions to get this running with the newer satellites?</div></blockquote>Keps file format got updated several months ago<br><br>Use the latest CPS and latest firmware, otherwise you are likely to have a data missmatch<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Mar 04, 2024 11:15 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
